"In Renjen-art'h's era, training facilities raised children to be bound, heedless of suitability."
"They taught knighthood as the only decent life, cut outside contact, and bound children early."
"Hundreds of thousands were churned through them."
"Renjen, among the mightiest Artonans ever, sired at least sixteen hundred children to fill them."
"Among his last were the Primary, Alis and Tesen, raised in the art'h dormitory by Murmur."
"Survivors of that generation find it repulsive; oaths and choosing seasons are what they lacked."
"Now the lives of young knights are held precious."
